<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archduke John of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1782–1859</span> · Also known as Archduke Johann of Austria, Archduke John</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">John of Austria</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> prince, son of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany">Leopold II</a>, who commanded Austrian armies against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and was a popular patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>. His liberal reputation and marriage to a postmaster's daughter made him acceptable to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt-parliament">Frankfurt Parliament</a>, which elected him Imperial Regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1848. He held the office until the provisional central power was dissolved in 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archduke-john-of-austria.jpg" alt="Archduke John of Austria" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leopold Kupelwieser · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_Kupelwieser_-_Erzherzog_Johann.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
